# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# Added after every shell script in the repository became unparseable by bash:
#
#   lab/verify-safety-suite.sh: line 27: $'\r': command not found
#   lab/verify-safety-suite.sh: line 51: `run_case() {
#
# The project is authored on Windows and executed on Linux — in the container,
# in CI, and on every provider instance it will ever touch. Without this file,
# a Windows editor silently rewrites scripts with CRLF and bash refuses them.
#
# The cost of that was not theoretical. It broke:
#   - lab/verify-safety-suite.sh  — the mutation battery, i.e. the project's
#     entire claim that its safety suite can be shown to fail
#   - lab/docker/build.sh         — so the pinned container could never be
#     built, which is why zero evidence bundles were ever publishable
#   - lab/docker/run.sh           — so no probe could run in a container
#
# Text files are normalised to LF in the repository. Shell scripts and the
# Dockerfiles are pinned to LF explicitly, because a CRLF in those is not a
# cosmetic difference — it is a syntax error.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.cff       text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
.gitignore  text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.pdf       binary
